insert into public.drafts(id,slug,content,version,updated_at,published_at) values ('22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222','top-two-salaries-per-department','{"id":"22222222-2222-4222-8222-222222222222","slug":"top-two-salaries-per-department","title":"Top two salaries per department","summary":"Rank salaries within each team, while keeping employees who tie for a place.","difficulty":"Moderate","tags":["Window functions","CTEs","Ranking"],"isSample":true,"problem":"<p>Return all employees earning one of the two highest distinct salaries in their department. Include everyone tied at either salary level. Sort by department, descending salary, then employee name.</p><p>Assume salary is non-null. This query uses MySQL 8.0 or later.</p>","approach":"<p>Rank salary levels independently within each department. DENSE_RANK is a good fit because ties share a rank and do not create gaps. Use a CTE to filter the computed rank in an outer query.</p>","sql":"WITH ranked AS (\n    SELECT department, employee, salary,\n           DENSE_RANK() OVER (\n               PARTITION BY department\n               ORDER BY salary DESC\n           ) AS salary_rank\n    FROM employees\n)\nSELECT department, employee, salary\nFROM ranked\nWHERE salary_rank <= 2\nORDER BY department, salary DESC, employee;","explanation":"<ol><li>PARTITION BY department restarts the ranking for each team.</li><li>ORDER BY salary DESC assigns rank 1 to the highest salary.</li><li>Engineering has ranks 1, 1, 2, 3. Both employees earning 90000 stay in the result.</li><li>The CTE makes salary_rank available for the WHERE clause in the outer SELECT.</li></ol>","takeaways":"<p>Choose the ranking function based on the question. ROW_NUMBER would keep just two people. RANK can skip the second salary level after a tie. DENSE_RANK keeps the two highest distinct salaries.</p>","alternative":"","performance":"<p>Window functions may require sorting. An index on (department, salary) may help some access patterns, but verify the actual execution plan. Select only the columns you need.</p>","before":[{"id":"s4","name":"employees","columns":["department","employee","salary"],"rows":[["Engineering","Asha","90000"],["Engineering","Dev","90000"],["Engineering","Mira","80000"],["Engineering","Rohan","70000"],["Sales","Leena","65000"],["Sales","Noor","60000"],["Sales","Tara","50000"]]}],"after":[{"id":"s5","name":"result","columns":["department","employee","salary"],"rows":[["Engineering","Asha","90000"],["Engineering","Dev","90000"],["Engineering","Mira","80000"],["Sales","Leena","65000"],["Sales","Noor","60000"]]}]}'::jsonb,1,'2026-01-02T10:00:00Z','2026-01-02T10:00:00Z') on conflict do nothing;
